course: dictionary
lesson: 7328
title: Learning from context: planetarium
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A planetarium is a place where the night sky is shown on a curved ceiling, so people can learn about space. You may not know this word at first, but the words around it can help. Read the sentence again and look for clues.
explain: «Scientists found that some beetles kept a straight line in a planetarium, a dome-shaped room that shows the night sky on its ceiling.» The words after the comma explain the word. A dome-shaped room that shows the night sky is a good match for planetarium. Check by putting your meaning in place of the word: "in a dome-shaped room that shows the night sky" still makes sense.
explain: «Experiments in a planetarium showed birds steering by the stars.» Here the stars are shown inside a building, and scientists test animals there. This tells you a planetarium is a place for learning about the night sky, not a place for keeping planets.
fact: A planetarium is a building with a round, domed ceiling where pictures of stars, planets and the night sky are shown.
fact: Planetarium can also mean the machine that projects the sky onto the dome.
fact: The plural of planetarium can be planetariums or planetaria.
fact: In a planetarium show, you sit under the dome and look up to see the stars and planets.
fact: Scientists use planetariums to test animals, such as birds steering by the stars around the North Star.
exercise: «The planetarium is a dome-shaped room that shows the night sky on its ceiling.» What is a planetarium in this sentence? | A kind of beetle that rolls balls of dung | A tall tower by the sea | *A dome-shaped room that shows the night sky on its ceiling | A shop that sells telescopes
exercise: Ella says a planetarium is a zoo for stars. What does planetarium really mean? | A small telescope you hold in your hand | A zoo where stars are kept in cages | A ship that sails across the sky | *A building with a domed ceiling where the night sky is shown
exercise: Which is NOT a plural of planetarium? | planetaria | planetariums | *planetarys
test: «Experiments in a planetarium showed birds steering by the stars around the North Star.» What does this tell you about a planetarium? | It is a river that birds fly over | It is a kind of food that birds eat | *It can show a night sky with stars, so scientists can test animals | It is a place where birds are kept in cages
test: Which group of words is about space? | *stars, planets and constellations | beetles, dung and balls | rain, snow and fog | bread, butter and jam
exam: «A planetarium is a dome-shaped room that shows the night sky on its ceiling.» Using this clue, what is a planetarium? | A huge tent for camping under the stars | A park where you can feed birds | *A room with a domed ceiling that shows the night sky | A machine that makes rain
